---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { contatti, azienda } from '../../dati';
---

<Base
  titolo="Privacy policy | mitis"
  descrizione="How mitis.dev handles data: no cookies, no tracking, only the emails you choose to send us."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="contenuto" class="px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-5">privacy</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-h2 font-bold">Privacy policy.</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-body text-carta/80">
        <p>
          The short version: this site collects no data. No cookies, no analytics, no pixels, no
          requests to third parties. The long version is below, and it's still short.
        </p>
        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-l font-bold text-carta">Data controller</h2>
        <p>
          mitis · VAT no. (P.IVA) {azienda.pIva} · <a
            href={`mailto:${contatti.email}`}
            class="text-lichene underline underline-offset-4 hover:no-underline"
            >{contatti.email}</a
          >
        </p>
        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-l font-bold text-carta">Browsing</h2>
        <p>
          The site is static and sets no cookies, and it uses no tracking or profiling tools. It
          is hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.): as with any hosting, the servers may record
          technical logs (IP address, user agent) for security and operational reasons. That
          processing is described in{' '}
          <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
            class="text-lichene underline underline-offset-4 hover:no-underline"
            >GitHub's privacy statement</a
          >.
        </p>
        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-l font-bold text-carta">If you write to us</h2>
        <p>
          If you contact us by email, we process the data you choose to send (your address, the
          content of the message) for the sole purpose of replying and managing any resulting
          relationship. No automatic mailing-list signups, no marketing use, no sharing with
          third parties.
        </p>
        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-l font-bold text-carta">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can request access to, rectification or erasure of your data, and
          lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection authority (Garante per la
          protezione dei dati personali). For any request, an email is enough.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
